# Monitor: LIKWID overlay (Grace / aarch64 hybrid)

**Activation:** when editing LIKWID overlay sources, `cpu_counter_metrics*`, or aarch64 static/configure paths that enable `MONITOR_CPU_LIKWID_OVERLAY`.

## Hybrid ownership (same `host_cpu_hw` type)

| Source | Keys |
|--------|------|
| **`arm` backend** (no DCGM since round 2) | `cpu_util_*_accum_us` (from `/proc/stat` jiffies; clock from cpufreq `scaling_cur_freq` — `monitor-dcgm-integration.mdc`), `arm_dram_bw_bytes`; socket power is the separate `host_power_socket` type; **fail-soft** `cpu_clock_est_cycles` (= **active** util×freq), `aperf` (=act), `mperf` (=ref) |
| **LIKWID overlay** | Overwrites `aperf` / `mperf` / `cpu_clock_est_cycles` **only when measured cycles &gt; 0**; owns `fp_arith_inst_retired_scalar_*`, `arm_est_flops` (= SP+DP only), `arm_int8_ops`, `arm_int16_ops`, optional `instr_retired` |

- aarch64 **`auto` is `--with-cpu-counter-backend=arm`** (the `dcgm` value was removed in round 2, no alias). LIKWID overlay is an additive layer (`MONITOR_CPU_LIKWID_OVERLAY`), not a separate exclusive backend. Exclusive `--with-cpu-counter-backend=likwid` is allowed on ARM and **loses the `/proc/stat` util accumulators**.
- **`cpu_counter_metrics_likwid_ready()` on `arm` builds** must remain declared and defined (stub **returns 0**). Exclusive-backend ready is **not** overlay-ready; x86 uncore/RAPL callers under `HAVE_LIKWID` must still see a prototype (Horizon rpmbuild regression).
- **Fail-soft cycles (mandatory on Grace):** always accumulate and publish util×freq estimates even when `MONITOR_CPU_LIKWID_OVERLAY` is set: **`cpu_clock_est_cycles` and `aperf` = active** (flat when util≈0); **`mperf` = reference** (wall×freq). Overlay must **not** clear those keys when measured cycles are 0. Do **not** publish synthesized FLOPs/instr under overlay (SP/DP/`arm_est_flops` stay overlay-owned).
- Emit contract: every overlay collect that has SP/DP must set **both** scalar keys **and** `arm_est_flops = SP + DP`. Do **not** fold int8/int16 into `arm_est_flops`.
- Integer ops: map only when the eventset programs them; production Grace eventset is **CYC+INS only** (`CPU_CYCLES:PMC0,INST_RETIRED:PMC1`) with CYC-only fallback. Packed 128/256/512 FP buckets stay 0 unless a future event maps them.
- **Grace DRAM CAS (`arm_aarch64_imc`)**: the overlay first tries `likwid_arch_eventset_grace_scf()` = CYC+INS **plus** `CMEM_RD_DATA:SCF0,CMEM_WR_TOTAL_BYTES:SCF1` in the **same** group (no second uncore group, no per-tick re-arm). When it succeeds, `cpu_counter_metrics_likwid_overlay_has_scf()` is 1 and `arm_imc.c` reads one device per socket (`scf<N>`, lead CPU from `nvidia_scf_pmu_<N>/cpumask`, `arm_imc_scf.c`) via `likwid_pmc_adapter_read_event`, accumulating lifetime `E` with `likwid_overlay_lifetime_advance`; units are 64-byte CAS (reads = 32 B beats / 2, writes = bytes / 64). Use `cmem_*` only — `gmem_*` is GPU memory. The overlay begins inside `arm_backend_begin`, so `stats_runtime.c` must begin `host_cpu_hw` first on overlay builds too (`STATS_RUNTIME_BEGIN_CPU_HW_FIRST`; registry order puts `arm_aarch64_imc` first — c122-018 regression: no rows all run; locked by `test_stats_runtime_overlay_begin_order`). The overlay can still come up after `arm_aarch64_imc` began, so `arm_imc.c` must **not** disable itself when SCF PMUs exist but the overlay is not up yet: `arm_imc_scf_begin_mode` returns `PENDING` (type stays enabled, 0 devices) and collect attaches via `arm_imc_scf_collect_mode` on the first tick `has_scf()` is 1. When the SCF eventset fails setup, the ladder falls back to CYC+INS, then CYC only, and **keep** `arm_imc.c`'s perf `dmc`/`imc` scan as the fallback. The util×freq `arm_dram_bw_bytes` estimate stays as a second source (user decision 2026-11-03).

## Static link

- Build static `liblikwid.a` (+ hwloc + lua) via `scripts/build_static_bundle.sh` `build_likwid()` on **all** arches (`STATIC_PIN_LIKWID_*`; pin **5.5.2**, `ACCESSMODE=perf_event`, `-fPIC`).
- `configure.ac` probes `perfmon_init` for exclusive LIKWID **and** the arm (non-x86) overlay.
- `prepare_rpmbuild_dirs.sh` requires `liblikwid*.a` on **all** arches. Do **not** require `libpapi.a`.

## Runtime

- Eventset ladder: `likwid_arch_eventset_grace_scf()`, then `likwid_arch_eventset_grace()`, then `likwid_arch_eventset_grace_cyc_only()` on setup failure. The first rung comes from `likwid_arch_eventset_grace_first(getenv("HPCPERFSTATS_LIKWID_GRACE_SCF"))`: exactly `"0"` starts at CYC+INS (no SCF; `has_scf()` 0; logs `SCF uncore events off (HPCPERFSTATS_LIKWID_GRACE_SCF=0)`). That knob is **measurement-only** — the overhead harness's `arm_cpu_noscf` VARIANT leg sets it in its runtime drop-in to cost SCF (`monitor-overhead-measurement.mdc` law 10); never set it in the shipped unit, sysconfig or site conf, and keep the log text in sync with `driver_map.VARIANTS` (`test_overlay_build_groups_imc_with_dcgm_cpu_and_offers_noscf_variant`). `cpu_counter_metrics_likwid_ready()` on `arm` builds stays the stub `0` — Grace SCF does not go through `likwid_uncore_adapter`.
- Overlay init fail: **do not** disable `host_cpu_hw`; `/proc/stat` util stays. Exclusive ARM LIKWID still fail-closes the type.
- Collect: one `prepare_collect` + `read_group` per tick; per-CPU `read_cpu_cycles_instr` must not re-`readGroupCounters`.
- **ARM / Grace no per-tick re-arm:** `likwid_pmc_adapter_prepare_collect()` must **not** call `perfmon_setupCounters` / `perfmon_startCounters` on aarch64/ARM. Those re-arms exist only for **x86** core-group recovery after DF/IMC/RAPL steal. Re-arming on Grace resets the PERF window and publishes last-interval counts for schema **`E`** keys (`cpu_clock_est_cycles` / `aperf` / `mperf` / `instr_retired`). After begin, ARM collect is `read_group` + per-CPU peek; overlay advances a **lifetime** total via `likwid_overlay_lifetime_advance` (absolute when readings grow; sticky add-on-drop if the window resets; raw `0` must not clear the total). Keep x86 per-tick re-arm unchanged.
- `HPCPERFSTATS_LIKWID_ACCESS=direct` is still rejected (PERF only) on ARM too.
- Keep collect hot-path bounded; do not add unbounded per-sample work.

## Overlap

- **`monitor-dcgm-integration.mdc`** — Grace CPU off DCGM, `host_power_socket`, GPU NVML/DCGM path; hybrid fail-soft cycles + LIKWID measured overwrite.
- **`monitor-amd-epyc-likwid.mdc`** — exclusive x86 LIKWID (Intel/AMD); overlay does not own IMC/DF/RAPL.
- **`monitor-local-build-deps.mdc`** / **`monitor-static-build-verification.mdc`** — static PREFIX pins.
- **`monitor-emitted-variable-naming.mdc`** — portable key names.
